,"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.8.dev7.official [c971f93e7]\n- Not Reproducible in v4.7.2.stable.official [ed1daf0bf]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev7 - Android 16 (SDK 36 build OS3.0.307.0.WPJCNXM) - Single-window, 1 monitor (2600x1268 @ 120.00 Hz) - OpenGL ES 3 (Compatibility) - Mali-G720 MC8 - MT6899 (8 threads) - Android (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nUsing the android runtime to get window insets causes project to crash on start in the editor with no errors. I needed that to access corner radius, based on the example code from:\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14056#issuecomment-3816832522\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Setup project and add the following script to the root control node\n```gdscript\nextends Control\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tEngine.get_singleton(\"AndroidRuntime\").getActivity().getWindow().getDecorView().getRootWindowInsets()\n\n```\n2. Launch the project and observe the project immediately stops with no error/warnings\n\n**4.8 dev7**\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ad0ebd5a-7529-457f-9366-17c5085045f2\n\n**4.7.2** \n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7ad3d535-6601-439d-ae2c-6d4d47564cb0\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[get-rounded-android.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32987402/get-rounded-android.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124123/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124123/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}